  "title": "Bank of England Rises Interest Rates Amid Inflation and Energy Pressures",
  "summary": "The Bank of England raised its benchmark interest rate to 4% for the first time since 2023, signaling a response to inflation and energy costs. The Bank also warned of further hikes if global energy prices remain high.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Bank of England raised its key rate to 4% from 3.75% in response to inflation and energy costs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Bank of England maintained its interest rates at 3.75% despite rising inflation and energy costs, while the Bank of England defied the Federal Reserve's rate-hike lead.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Bank of England's monetary policy committee voted for a rate increase, with one policymaker preferring a more dramatic half-point increase.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
