      "title": "Bank of England raises interest rates to 4%, the first increase for more than three years",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/05/bank-of-england-raises-interest-rates-first-increase-for-more-than-three-years",
      "description": "<p>Base rate increases from 3.75% and Bank governor signals another rise in near future to combat rising inflation</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/05/interest-rate-rise-in-midst-of-cost-of-living-crisis-will-leave-many-incredulous\">Analysis: Interest rate rise in midst of cost of living crisis will leave many incredulous</a></p></li></ul><p>The Bank of England has raised interest rates for the first time in three years and warned of another increase to combat inflationary pressure unleashed by the Iran war.</p><p>Eight members of the Bank’s monetary policy committee (MPC) voted for the rise, which takes the base rate from 3.75% to 4%. The ninth member, Catherine Mann, preferred a more dramatic half-point increase.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/05/bank-of-england-raises-interest-rates-first-increase-for-more-than-three-years\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
